    <h1>Spinosaurus</h1>
    <hr>

    <h2>Overview & Time Period</h2>
    <p>The Spinosaurus was a massive carnivorous predator that lived during the Cretaceous period, roughly 95 to 93 million years ago. It is widely recognized as one of the largest meat-eating dinosaurs discovered to date.</p>

    <h2>Physical Traits & Adaptations</h2>
    <p>A distinctive physical feature of the Spinosaurus was the large, sail-like structure made of tall neural spines along its back. It also featured a long, crocodile-like snout lined with straight, conical teeth and dense bones.</p>

    <h2>Diet & Lifestyle</h2>
    <p>Unlike most large predatory theropods that operated purely as land hunters, evidence indicates that the Spinosaurus had a semi-aquatic lifestyle. Its anatomical adaptations made it an expert at swimming and hunting large fish and aquatic prey in ancient river and swamp systems.</p>

